  "summary": "SprySOCKS is a FishMonger backdoor, previously Linux-only, that now has two Windows variants: WIN_DRV, which uses the RawWNPF kernel driver to hide its connections, processes, files and registry keys and to divert TCP traffic, and WIN_PLUS, which persists as a print processor. Both are delivered via DLL side-loading, decrypt their components from AES-ECB-encrypted .dat containers, inject the backdoor into svchost.exe via process doppelgänging, and speak a custom TCP/UDP/WebSocket C&C protocol with more than 30 commands.",
